# PowerShell 5.1 (the version shipped with Windows) assumes CP1252 for a .ps1
# with no BOM, so a single non-ASCII byte breaks parsing before the script
# runs. Found on a real Windows deployment 2026-09-07: all five wrappers were
# unrunnable because of em-dashes in their comments. Keep them ASCII, and
# never let git rewrite their line endings either.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf working-tree-encoding=UTF-8
*.bat text eol=crlf
